{"status":"completed","summary":"Inventory application is served on node1 over TCP/8181 with SELinux enforcing. Apache, SELinux policy, and firewalld configuration persisted across the required node restart.","actions_performed":["Installed and enabled Apache HTTP Server.","Created the inventory application and dedicated port-8181 virtual host.","Assigned TCP/8181 to SELinux type http_port_t.","Allowed TCP/8181 through firewalld persistently.","Restarted node1 and verified full recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Serve the inventory application over TCP/8181 while mandatory access control remains enforcing","command_ids":["cmd-edf1392057d84375","cmd-5b05ea2fd1f7495c","cmd-9c00196ca86b49ee"],"summary":"SELinux reports Enforcing; 8181 is labeled http_port_t; Apache is enabled and active; the listener is bound on 8181; firewalld allows the port; and an HTTP request to the node IP returns the inventory application."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-19d0d80ffcbf4b5c","cmd-224ace20fe50487e","cmd-fbdf1f3b15694f37","cmd-9c00196ca86b49ee"],"summary":"Pre-restart boot identity and healthy application state were captured, the safe reboot was acknowledged, boot identity changed from fbdf5b2c-bb43-49f6-935d-fb98f8a972f6 to 168ab3ad-bf7b-4be0-8c68-05bf8f82cd0e, and post-restart checks confirmed enforcing SELinux, active Apache, the 8181 listener, persistent policy/firewall rules, application data, and no HTTPD SELinux denials."}]}
